If an opioid-taper for a patient has an opioid-discontinuation-goal then every clinician should openly discuss the opioid-discontinuation-goal with the patient.
If an opioid-taper for a patient has a benefit-risk-favorable-opioid-reduction-goal then every clinician should openly discuss the benefit-risk-favorable-opioid-reduction-goal with the patient.
Every clinician should individualize a taper-goal for a patient with an individualized-benefit-risk-assessment.
Every clinician should consider a patient-circumstance during an individualized-benefit-risk-assessment.
